# Ownership for the paths where an unreviewed change can silently break the
# product or the release pipeline. GitHub requests a review from the matching
# owner automatically; it does not block a merge on its own.
#
# Keep this narrow: ownership on every file trains reviewers to ignore the
# request. Runtime engine, API wiring, CI and release are the high-blast-radius
# paths; docs and frontend are not listed on purpose.

# Runtime engine: memory scoring, lifecycle, decay, admission.
/server/core/engine/    @ali-ulu

# Server entrypoint and API wiring: routing, auth boundary, middleware.
/server/api.py          @ali-ulu
/server/auth.py         @ali-ulu
/server/routes/         @ali-ulu

# Release pipeline: workflows and the version bump tooling.
/.github/workflows/     @ali-ulu
/scripts/release.py     @ali-ulu

# Packaging: dependencies and build metadata shipped to users.
/pyproject.toml         @ali-ulu
